# dms-tenant bench environment reference (Videojet OEM deployment)
# ================================================================
# This file is a CHECKLIST of every env var the merged compose yaml
# references. The actual values live in TWO places, NEVER in git:
#
#   1. Dokploy UI → dms-uat (or dms) application → Environment tab
#      → paste each KEY=VALUE pair from below with real values.
#      Dokploy injects them at container start.
#
#   2. ~/gitops/traefik-routes.yaml on the MANAGER VPS
#      → SITES_RULE domains go here (Traefik routing).
#
# Generating the compose yaml to upload to Dokploy (LOCAL machine):
#
#   docker compose \
#     -f compose.yaml \
#     -f overrides/compose.redis.yaml \
#     -f overrides/compose.agent.yaml \
#     config --no-interpolate > /tmp/dms.yaml
#
# IMPORTANT: --no-interpolate keeps ${VAR} placeholders intact so
# Dokploy's Environment tab substitutes them at runtime. Without
# --no-interpolate, docker compose resolves ${VAR} locally and bakes
# secrets into the file you upload — Dokploy's Environment tab would
# then be unused and rotation would require regenerating the yaml.
#
# Paste /tmp/dms.yaml into Dokploy → New Application → Docker Compose,
# then fill in the Environment tab from the KEY=VALUE list below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Image -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker Hub image built by GitHub Actions (.github/workflows/build-dms*.yml)
CUSTOM_IMAGE=svasamm/dms-tenant

# Floating tags (auto-updated by CI on each release — no config change needed):
#   uat-latest   — always points to latest UAT build  (use for UAT bench)
#   latest       — always points to latest production build (use for prod bench)
#
# Pinned tags (immutable, for rollback or audit):
#   uat-v0.1.0-abc1234   — exact UAT build  (use to roll back to a known-good)
#   v1.0.0-abc1234       — exact production build
#
# For UAT:
CUSTOM_TAG=uat-latest
# For Production:
# CUSTOM_TAG=latest

# always  = pull on every container start (use for floating tags like uat-latest)
# missing = only pull if image not present locally (use for pinned SHA tags)
PULL_POLICY=always

# --- Database ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Must match DB_PASSWORD in mariadb.env on the SHARED MariaDB container
DB_HOST=mariadb-database
DB_PORT=3306
DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_SAME_AS_MARIADB_ENV

# --- Bench identity ----------------------------------------------------------
# ROUTER: unique name for this bench. Used as:
#   - Docker network name for this bench's internal network
#   - Must be unique per agent (two benches on the same agent need different names)
#
# UAT  → ROUTER=dms-uat
# Prod → ROUTER=dms
ROUTER=dms-uat

# --- Agent routing (Option B: Central Traefik on Manager) -------------------
# AGENT_PRIVATE_IP: Hostinger private network IP of the Agent VPS this bench runs on.
#   Same Agent as Lucoze (10.0.0.2) — Videojet co-tenants with Lucoze.
AGENT_PRIVATE_IP=10.0.0.2

# BENCH_PORT: Port the frontend container listens on (on the private network).
#   Must be unique per bench on the SAME agent. Different agents can share ports.
#
# Current per-agent allocation (see gitops/README.md port table):
#   cafirm            = 8080
#   lucoze-admin      = 8082
#   lucoze (tenant)   = 8083
#   lucoze-website    = 8084
#   dms-uat           = 8085    ← UAT for this bench
#   dms (prod)        = 8086    ← Production for this bench
#
# For UAT:
BENCH_PORT=8085
# For Production:
# BENCH_PORT=8086

# --- Domains (for reference — used in Manager Traefik config, not here) -----
# SITES_RULE is NOT used in compose.agent.yaml (no Traefik labels on agent).
# Keep it here as documentation for what to put in ~/gitops/traefik-routes.yaml
# on the Manager.
#
# UAT  example: Host(`uat.videojet.svasamm.com`)
# Prod example: Host(`videojet.svasamm.com`)
SITES_RULE=Host(`CHANGE_ME.yourdomain.com`)
